171	african_arguments	168	https://africanarguments.org/2026/08/two-presidents-no-government-why-tigrays-war-is-coming-back/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=two-presidents-no-government-why-tigrays-war-is-coming-back	Two Presidents, No Government: Why Tigray’s War Is Coming Back <p>In Mekelle, the capital of Ethiopia&#8217;s northern Tigray region, two men call themselves president. One is Lieutenant General Tadesse Worede, appointed with Addis Ababa&#8217;s approval to run the region until elections could be held. The other is Debretsion Gebremichael, chairman of the party that governed Tigray for decades and led it through a war (2020-2022) that killed an estimated 600,000 people and displaced two to three million. On 5 May, a regional council that had not met in more than three years reunited and elected him. Addis Ababa treats that council as an illegal body: it was abolished under the [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://africanarguments.org/2026/08/two-presidents-no-government-why-tigrays-war-is-coming-back/">Two Presidents, No Government: Why Tigray&#8217;s War Is Coming Back</a> appeared first on <a href="https://africanarguments.org">African Arguments</a>.</p>	en	\N	\N	https://africanarguments.org/2026/08/two-presidents-no-government-why-tigrays-war-is-coming-back/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=two-presidents-no-government-why-tigrays-war-is-coming-back	2026-08-03 16:17:19+00	2026-08-06 12:54:05.090777+00	african_arguments:Nigeria diaspora community UK	neutral	-0.0036	[{"text": "Two Presidents", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "No Government", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Why Tigray", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "War Is Coming Back", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "In Mekelle", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Ethiopia", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Tigray", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "One", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Lieutenant General Tadesse Worede", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Addis Ababa", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "The", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Debretsion Gebremichael", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "African Arguments", "label": "PERSON"}]	["tigray", "presidents", "coming", "region", "addis", "three", "council", "mekelle", "capital", "ethiopia"]	["political_engagement"]	t	2026-08-06 12:55:01.723123+00
173	african_arguments	170	https://africanarguments.org/2026/08/how-russia-lost-the-ability-to-leave-the-central-african-republic/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=how-russia-lost-the-ability-to-leave-the-central-afri	How Russia Lost the Ability to Leave the Central African Republic <p>When armed groups attacked the border post of Am-Dafok in northeastern CAR on 30 June 2026, most analysts asked the familiar question: who was behind the attack, and how resilient is Russia’s presence? The right question is different. Why can Russia not simply leave the Central African Republic — even if it wanted to? The answer changes how we understand the nature of external military presence in post-patronage Africa. Not Wagner, Not Africa Corps: A System. The debate over whether the transition from Wagner to Africa Corps is complete misses the point. The rebranding is real. The architecture did not [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://africanarguments.org/2026/08/how-russia-lost-the-ability-to-leave-the-central-african-republic/">How Russia Lost the Ability to Leave the Central African Republic</a> appeared first on <a href="https://africanarguments.org">African Arguments</a>.</p>	en	\N	\N	https://africanarguments.org/2026/08/how-russia-lost-the-ability-to-leave-the-central-african-republic/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=how-russia-lost-the-ability-to-leave-the-central-african-republic	2026-08-03 10:52:32+00	2026-08-06 12:54:05.114698+00	african_arguments:Nigeria diaspora community UK	neutral	0.0712	[{"text": "How Russia Lost", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Ability", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Leave", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Central African Republic", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "When", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Dafok", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Russia", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "The", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Why", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Not Wagner", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Not Africa Corps", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "System", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Wagner", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Africa Corps", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "African Arguments", "label": "PERSON"}]	["russia", "african", "leave", "central", "republic", "africa", "lost", "ability", "question", "presence"]	[]	t	2026-08-06 12:55:02.242041+00
