169	african_arguments	166	https://africanarguments.org/2026/08/the-winter-circus-a-memoir/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=the-winter-circus-a-memoir	The Winter Circus: A Memoir <p>The Winter Circus: A Memoir (2026) by Leo Zeilig is published by the Uganda-based Editor House Facility (EHF). A genre-defying work blending memoir, fiction, and political reflection, it explores what it means to live through personal and global crisis. Moving between intimate experience and wider social forces, it captures a world of deep contradiction: extreme wealth alongside poverty, rising global movements alongside fragmentation. Set across Europe and Africa, it tells of a world on the cusp of radical change. The story takes place over a weekend in Paris. Four friends, Ivan, Louis, Patrice and Bhaskar travel to the French capital to [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://africanarguments.org/2026/08/the-winter-circus-a-memoir/">The Winter Circus: A Memoir</a> appeared first on <a href="https://africanarguments.org">African Arguments</a>.</p>	en	\N	\N	https://africanarguments.org/2026/08/the-winter-circus-a-memoir/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=the-winter-circus-a-memoir	2026-08-04 11:35:46+00	2026-08-06 12:54:05.068551+00	african_arguments:Nigeria diaspora community UK	neutral	0.045	[{"text": "The Winter Circus", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Memoir", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Leo Zeilig", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Uganda", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Editor House Facility", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Moving", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Set", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Europe", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "The", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Paris", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Four", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Ivan", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Louis", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Patrice", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Bhaskar", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "French", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "African Arguments", "label": 